To be absurd, the increment and decrement operators can be overloaded in C++
so even if the order of evaluation were defined you couldn't guarantee the 
results.

(It would be incredibly stupid, but you could define ++ and -- to return
the left and right branches of a binary tree, the "previous" and "next"
pointer of a doubly-linked list, etc.  Toss in the fact that the _prefix_
and _suffix_ forms are two different functions...

